      "readme_excerpt": "# shivamshashank.github.io\n\nPersonal site. Served by GitHub Pages from `main` at the repository root.\n\nPlain HTML and CSS in a single file. No build step, no dependencies, no\npackage manager. Edit `index.html`, push, done.\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nindex.html    the whole site — markup, styles and script\nimg/          every image the page uses\nLICENSE\n```\n\n## Images\n\n```\nimg/profile.png             header photo\nimg/cloudgraph.png          CloudGraph topology screenshot (card header)\nimg/cloudgraph-results.png  unsupported-claim-rate chart (inline figure)\nimg/microglucometer.webp    MicroGlucoMeter workflow diagram (card header)\nimg/hpe.png                 experience / education badges\nimg/unbox.png\nimg/uob.png\nimg/iitj.png\n```\n\nTwo different behaviours, worth knowing before you rename anything:\n\n- **Photo and badges** are loaded by a small script that only swaps the image in\n  once it has loaded. If the file is missing, the initials placeholder stays and\n  nothing breaks. The badge script derives the filename from each badge's\n  `data-logo` attribute, so `data-logo=\"hpe\"` looks for `img/hpe.png`.\n- **Project images** are plain `<img>` tags. A missing or renamed file here\n  *will* show a brok",
